      en: "Jubilee Palace (National Palace) in Addis Ababa was the official residence of Emperor Haile Selassie. Built in the 1950s for his Silver Jubilee, it is a modernist building with traditional Ethiopian accents. It hosted state receptions and diplomatic meetings. After the 1974 revolution, it became the government seat. Today, it houses the Prime Minister's office. Surrounded by manicured gardens, it symbolizes both imperial heritage and modern governance.",
