      en: "The Red Terror Martyrs' Memorial in Asmara, Eritrea, was inaugurated in 2011 to honor those killed during the Ethiopian Derg regime (1974-1987). The memorial features a 20-meter granite stele and an underground museum. Names of the victims are engraved on the walls. The museum displays photographs, documents, and personal effects. It serves as a site for annual commemorations. The memorial is a symbol of the struggle for freedom. It is a tourist attraction and a place for education about human rights.",
