      en: "The Royal Enclosure in Gondar, also known as Fasil Ghebbi, was the imperial residence of Ethiopian emperors in the 17th century. Built by Emperor Fasilides (1632–1667), it includes several castles, churches, and palaces. The architecture blends Ethiopian, Portuguese, and Indian styles. The complex is surrounded by a 900-meter-long wall. The most prominent building is Fasilides' Castle, with its turreted battlements. The site was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1979. The church of Debre Berhan Selassie inside features remarkable ceiling frescoes.",
